# Local defaults, loaded by `npm run dev`. Copy to .env to override — .env is gitignored and .env
# is loaded last, so it wins. Neither file overrides a variable already set in the shell.
#
# Real secrets never live in the repo. In staging and prod every value here comes from Secret
# Manager through infra/set-secret.sh (SPEC.md, "Security defaults"; ADR-0003).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://dona:dona@127.0.0.1:5434/dona
PORT=3000

# The golden set embeds through the real provider (`npm run evals`, `npm run measure`). Absent, the
# retrieval and grounding cases skip and say so; CI sets REQUIRE_EMBEDDINGS=1 so there they fail
# instead. Never a value in this file — export it in your shell, or leave it unset and let them skip.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# The docs bucket (slice 3.2). Deliberately unset here: locally there is no bucket, so
# createConfiguredStore falls back to the in-memory store and src/serve.ts prints `docs: memory` on
# the boot line. In staging and prod the deploy injects it (DOCS_BUCKET=dona-v5-<env>-docs), and a
# deployed revision whose boot line says `memory` is as wrong as a `-dev` version string.
# DOCS_BUCKET=

# The Document AI OCR processor (slice 4.1). Unset here on the same argument: locally there is no
# processor, createConfiguredOcr returns unconfigured, and src/serve.ts prints `ocr: unconfigured`.
# Staging and prod inject DOCUMENT_AI_PROCESSOR (looked up by display name dona-ocr-<env> in eu).
# The version is a config_settings row, not this file.
# DOCUMENT_AI_PROCESSOR=
# DOCUMENT_AI_LOCATION=eu
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=dona-v5

# Google sign-in (slice 5.1b). Deliberately unset here: with no OAuth client
# createConfiguredIdentity returns unconfigured, src/serve.ts prints `identity: unconfigured` on the
# boot line, and /staff/login says so rather than starting a redirect to nowhere. To sign in
# locally, put the two values in .env (gitignored) — the client is created by hand in the Cloud
# console, and its authorised redirect URI must be exactly
# http://127.0.0.1:3000/staff/auth/callback. Staging and prod inject both from Secret Manager
# (<env>-google-oauth-client-id / -secret, through infra/set-secret.sh). Never a value in this file.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The Workspace domain to require, when Dona Dom's answer lands (open question 12). Unset means the
# allowlist in staff_account is the only fence, which is the honest default until it does.
# STAFF_GOOGLE_HD=
# Where Google is told to send an operator back. Absent, the request's own origin is used, which is
# what `npm run dev` wants. The deploy sets it to the revision's own URL.
# STAFF_BASE_URL=
